%%
%%  MERMAID NOTATION LIMITATIONS (documented, not defects):
%%   1. Mermaid has no native UML use-case diagram type. Use-case models
%%      below are expressed as flowcharts using the conventions:
%%        ((text))  = use case (ellipse)
%%        [text]    = actor
%%        subgraph  = system boundary
%%        -.->|"<<include>>"|  /  -.->|"<<extend>>"|  = UML dependencies
%%        -.->|"<<generalization>>"| = actor generalisation
%%   2. Mermaid has no native DFD type. DFDs below use flowcharts with:
%%        ((text))  = process        [text]  = external entity
%%        [(text)]  = data store
%%   3. Mermaid stateDiagram-v2 does not render UML "final state" as a
%%      bullseye in all versions; [*] is used per Mermaid convention.
%%   4. Mermaid erDiagram does not express optionality beyond crow's-foot
%%      o/| markers; cardinality is therefore also stated in the SRS text.
%% =====================================================================


